<title>UK: TATE PEPPED UP BY RENEWED BID SPECULATION.</title>
<headline>TATE PEPPED UP BY RENEWED BID SPECULATION.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in food products group Tate &amp; Lyle rose on Friday as rumours of a possible bid from Associated British Foods were highlighted in the British press, dealers said.</p>
<p>Tate gained 5-1/2p to 419-1/2p whilst AB Foods was unchanged at 539-1/2p. On Thursday shares in Tate rose 8-1/2p.</p>
</text>
